    "body": "## Motivation\n\nWith `--export-metrics-to-file`, any request that carries `kv_hints` is missing from the exported metrics file.\n\n`GenerateReqInput` normalizes `kv_hints` into a `KvHintsEnvelope` (a `msgspec.Struct`), and `RequestMetricsExporter._format_output_data` passes the request fields to `json.dumps`, which can't encode it:\n\n```\nTypeError: Object of type KvHintsEnvelope is not JSON serializable\n```\n\n`FileRequestMetricsExporter.write_record` catches the error and only logs it (\"Failed to write perf metrics to file\"), so the record is silently dropped. `kv_hints` is not in `ALWAYS_EXCLUDE_FIELDS` or the exporter's skip lists.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `_format_output_data` passes `default=msgspec.to_builtins` to `json.dumps`, so msgspec structs in request fields are written as plain JSON (the envelope's dict form). Types that `msgspec.to_builtins` can't handle still raise `TypeError` as before.\n- New `test_serializes_kv_hints_envelope` in `test/registered/unit/observability/test_request_metrics_exporter.py`. It uses a local struct with the same shape as `KvHintsEnvelope`, because this file stubs `sglang.srt.managers` to stay free of heavy imports. It checks that `kv_hints` round-trips to the original dict. It fails on `main` with the `TypeError` above and passes with the change.\n\nI also ran a `write_record` repro with the real `decode_kv_hints_envelope`. On `main` it wrote 1 of 2 records; with the change it writes both, including the `kv_hints` dict.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot applicable: no model or kernel change.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable: `default` is only called for values `json` can't encode itself.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit). (`pre-commit run` on the changed files passes.)\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang